WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:10.830
An absolutely astonishing trailer for the
Godzilla sequel King of the Monsters just

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:11.830
dropped.

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:15.360
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and in this video I'm going to explain all

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:20.119
about the new monsters in the Godzilla 2 trailer
and I'll be revealing their special connection

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:23.560
with Millie Bobby Brown and Vera Farmiga's
characters.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:26.900
This image of a frozen King Ghidorah is simply
stunning.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:31.090
Now, we've known since we saw those paintings
of a dragon-like creature in the end credits

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:35.800
of Kong: Skull Island that King Ghidorah would
be appearing in this film, but this gorgeous

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:42.089
image of the three-headed winged serpent suspended
in icy Antarctica is still a delightful surprise.

00:00:42.089 --> 00:00:46.210
And that shot of him spreading his wings,
with the lightning behind him, is another

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:50.840
stunner because not only is Ghidorah's body
capable of conducting electrical currents,

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:56.190
but he also heats water vapour in the air
creating a localised but devastating storm

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:59.390
system with thunder and lightning as he travels.

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:03.520
Ghidorah was a powerful enemy of Godzilla,
Mothra and Rodan when he first appeared in

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:05.450
Ghidorah: The Three-Headed Monster.

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:10.430
In the 1964 Toho movie, the monstrous dragon
was an extra-terrestrial being that hatched

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:13.420
from an egg which initially appeared to be
a meteor.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:17.219
Ghidorah attempted to take over the Earth
until Mothra stood up to him, with Godzilla

00:01:17.219 --> 00:01:21.820
and Rodan eventually deciding to team up with
her to defeat Ghidorah and send him back to

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:22.820
space.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:26.909
So, I wonder if the filmmakers have gone with
an alien backstory for Ghidorah in the new

00:01:26.909 --> 00:01:27.909
movie.

00:01:27.909 --> 00:01:32.369
Then there's this majestic shot of Godzilla
rising from the sea and unleashing his "atomic

00:01:32.369 --> 00:01:36.551
breath", and as if that wasn't enough, it's
followed by a stunning shot of a beautiful

00:01:36.551 --> 00:01:41.430
bioluminescent Mothra in what looks like a
waterfall spreading her wings until she fills

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:46.189
the full screen with her wingspan which measures
over 800 feet.

00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:50.560
And shout-out to the haunting music, Debussy's
Claire de Lune, which works beautifully in

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:52.850
this moment and throughout the trailer.

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:57.119
As the name suggests, Mothra is a moth-like
creature that has often been portrayed as

00:01:57.119 --> 00:02:02.310
a saviour, and according to the Monarch Sciences
website, this version is a 'devastating guardian

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:07.149
angel' whose 'beta-wave bioluminescence […] can
be projected through the intricate patterns

00:02:07.149 --> 00:02:10.910
on its wings and weaponised into blinding
"god rays"'.

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:16.180
Mothra is one of movie studio Toho's most
popular kaiju and is surpassed only by Godzilla

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:18.460
in the number of movies that she's appeared
in.

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:25.280
She did go up against Godzilla in the 1964
movie Mothra vs Godzilla and also in 1992's

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:27.300
Godzilla vs Mothra.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:32.040
Next up is Rodan, a type of pteranodon that
first appeared on the big screen in Toho Studios'

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:37.980
1956 movie Rodan, and was initially a foe
of Godzilla's in the 1964 movie "Ghidorah:

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:39.700
The Three-Headed Monster".

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:44.800
In this film, Rodan has been lying dormant
in the Isla de Mona volcano, and we see this

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:49.080
"fire demon" returned to life in the trailer
as it sweeps over a city, leaving a trail

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:51.080
of destruction behind it.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:56.840
And that's because its 870-foot wingspan creates
a sonic thunderclap capable of levelling entire

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:59.050
cities as it flies overhead.

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:04.150
By the way, this gorgeous but devastating
image really reminded me of Game of Thrones.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.150
Speaking of which…

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:07.150
"Long live the King!"

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:10.330
Could that line have been any more Game of
Thrones?!

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:14.450
I feel like all Charles Dance is missing with
that dark, high-necked top he's wearing, is

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:16.480
his Hand of the King badge!

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:20.490
Details of Dance's character haven't been
revealed yet, but I wonder if he's part of

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:25.400
the mysterious organisation that's kidnapped
Millie Bobby Brown and Vera Farmiga's characters

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:28.670
and plans to use the creatures for its own
ends.

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:33.290
Obviously, any movie featuring Millie Bobbie
Brown and monsters is going to draw comparisons

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:34.760
with Stranger Things.

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:39.520
And this particular image here of Brown reaching
out to Mothra while her mother stands behind

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:43.180
her, reminded me of Eleven confronting the
Shadow Monster with Hopper.

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:47.130
By the looks of this scene though, Brown's
encounter with the creature seems a lot less

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:51.320
life-threatening than her monstrous face-to-face
in Stranger Things.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:56.520
In fact, speaking to EW, Brown said that once
her character Madison understands Godzilla,

00:03:56.520 --> 00:04:00.910
"there's some mutual respect for each other"
and she also added that Madison "has been

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:03.900
taught to not be scared of any monsters."

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:08.680
I imagine that will be because of her paleobiologist
mother, who works for the monster-tracking

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:10.300
organisation Monarch.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:14.920
Indeed, according to actress Vera Farmiga,
the character she plays "has figured out a

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:19.600
way to communicate with the creatures and
potentially control them using their bioacoustics

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:21.100
on a sonar level."

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:25.659
In contrast to the shot with Mothra, this
other image here seems a lot more menacing

00:04:25.659 --> 00:04:29.689
because although you might have thought that
was Godzilla in the background, look really

00:04:29.689 --> 00:04:35.300
carefully and you'll see three eyes meaning
that's actually the 3-headed Ghidorah looming

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:36.300
over Brown.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:40.960
I think Brown's character Madison will be
one of the keys to defeating Ghidorah alongside

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:43.380
Godzilla and the other monsters.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:47.270
And given Farmiga's words throughout the trailer,
I feel the movie's going to have a "people

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:49.300
are the real monsters" vibe.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.499
"Our world is changing."

00:04:51.499 --> 00:04:58.249
"The mass extinction we feared..."
"... has already begun."

00:04:58.249 --> 00:05:03.499
"And we are the cause."

00:05:03.499 --> 00:05:04.620
"We are the infection."

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:09.099
In fact, Farmiga has said that, for her, the
film is about saving the environment.

00:05:09.099 --> 00:05:13.449
So, what do you think about the Godzilla:
King of the Monsters trailer?

00:05:13.449 --> 00:05:17.620
And did you spot any other interesting details
or have any theories about the movie?

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:22.629
Let me know your thoughts below, and if you
enjoyed this, a thumbs-up is always appreciated.

00:05:22.629 --> 00:05:26.650
Tap left to check out more of my monster movie
playlist or tap right for another video you're

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:27.710
sure to like.

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:29.900
Thanks for watching and see ya next time.

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:31.120
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

